{"credits": [], "cve_id": null, "cvss": {"score": null, "vector_string": null}, "cvss_severities": {"cvss_v3": {"score": 0.0, "vector_string": null}, "cvss_v4": {"score": 8.7, "vector_string": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N"}}, "cwes": [{"cwe_id": "CWE-319", "name": "Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information"}, {"cwe_id": "CWE-494", "name": "Download of Code Without Integrity Check"}], "description": "The HTTP MCP server-registry backend factory (`atomic_agents/mcp_registry/http.py`, `make_http_mcp_server_registry_backend_from_url`) accepts both `http` and `https` schemes. Catalog entries carry `command`/`args` that are type-validated but content-unrestricted, and are later spawned as local stdio subprocesses by `MCPClientPool`. Over a cleartext `http://` catalog URL, a network man-in-the-middle can rewrite the catalog response to inject an arbitrary `command`/`args` and obtain code execution on the agent host, with no LLM involvement. The Policy MCP allowlist is not a default mitigation (`mcp_allow_fn` defaults to None), so absent an operator-authored allowlist every resolved spec connects.

**Affected:** `mcp_registry/http.py`, all versions through 1.0.0. (The `https` path is sound: `httpx` defaults to `verify=True`, `follow_redirects=False`.)

**Fix:** require `https` by default and gate `http://` behind a loud explicit opt-in. Defense-in-depth: allowlist the resolved command basename (or require confirmation) before any registry-sourced subprocess spawn. Document the consequence in spec/36.", "ghsa_id": "GHSA-xhcr-cqfr-m3hv", "github_reviewed_at": "2026-08-17T21:49:55Z", "html_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xhcr-cqfr-m3hv", "identifiers": [{"type": "GHSA", "value": "GHSA-xhcr-cqfr-m3hv"}], "nvd_published_at": null, "published_at": "2026-08-17T21:49:55Z", "references": ["https://github.com/dep0we/atomic-agents-stack/security/advisories/GHSA-xhcr-cqfr-m3hv", "https://github.com/dep0we/atomic-agents-stack/releases#release-v1.1.0", "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xhcr-cqfr-m3hv"], "repository_advisory_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/dep0we/atomic-agents-stack/security-advisories/GHSA-xhcr-cqfr-m3hv", "severity": "high", "source_code_location": "https://github.com/dep0we/atomic-agents-stack", "summary": "atomic-agents-stack: HTTP MCP catalog accepts cleartext http and spawns catalog-supplied commands (MITM to RCE)", "type": "reviewed", "updated_at": "2026-08-17T21:49:55Z", "url": "https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-xhcr-cqfr-m3hv", "vulnerabilities": [{"first_patched_version": "1.1.0", "package": {"ecosystem": "pip", "name": "atomic-agents-stack"}, "vulnerable_functions": [], "vulnerable_version_range": "<= 1.0.0"}], "withdrawn_at": null}
